1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,344
The Lunchbox Mix-Up.

3
00:00:03,344 --> 00:00:06,937
At lunch, Emma sits across from me and opens her sandwich.

4
00:00:06,937 --> 00:00:10,062
I open my blue lunchbox, expecting pasta.

5
00:00:10,062 --> 00:00:15,927
Inside, I find a giant salad, a small jar of dressing, and a note that says, Have a great meeting.

6
00:00:16,154 --> 00:00:16,823
Wow.

7
00:00:16,823 --> 00:00:19,208
Is your sandwich hiding under all that lettuce?

8
00:00:19,492 --> 00:00:21,465
I think I grabbed the wrong one.

9
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:24,298
Dad and I have exactly the same lunchbox.

10
00:00:24,298 --> 00:00:27,319
Mine was supposed to have pasta and apple slices.

11
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:31,098
So your dad is going to a meeting with apple slices and a dinosaur fork?

12
00:00:31,372 --> 00:00:33,480
I picture him opening the box.

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,595
Actually, he probably likes the dinosaur fork.

14
00:00:36,595 --> 00:00:40,595
I send Mom a message through the school office, just so nobody worries.

15
00:00:40,826 --> 00:00:42,380
I have an extra bread roll.

16
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,505
Would you like half?

17
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:44,961
Thanks.

18
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:47,440
I have plenty of cucumber if you want some.

19
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:52,284
We check that the food is okay for both of us, then put a clean napkin between our lunches.

20
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:53,443
Look at us.

21
00:00:53,443 --> 00:00:55,964
We accidentally opened a tiny restaurant.

22
00:00:56,236 --> 00:01:00,105
That afternoon, Dad is waiting at home with both empty lunchboxes.

23
00:01:00,105 --> 00:01:02,907
He holds up the dinosaur fork like a prize.

24
00:01:03,172 --> 00:01:04,843
Excellent pasta.

25
00:01:04,843 --> 00:01:06,916
Very professional fork.

26
00:01:06,916 --> 00:01:08,572
How was my salad?

27
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,062
Crunchy.

28
00:01:10,062 --> 00:01:11,593
Really crunchy.

29
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:13,656
Let's check the labels tomorrow.

30
00:01:13,924 --> 00:01:15,324
Good idea.

31
00:01:15,324 --> 00:01:18,136
Mine can say Dad, and yours can say Lucy.

32
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:22,447
Ben suggests a third label for himself: Person Who Would Like More Pasta.

33
00:01:22,447 --> 00:01:25,583
We give him a sticker, but we keep our lunchboxes.
